# TT.TICKET_INTERFACE -- change_deferral_date (S-TICKET-006: deferred ticket, non-deferred
# ticket, nonexistent ticket), update_ux_timeout_for_ticket (S-TICKET-011/012: every branch
# of the timeout table -- incident initial/non-initial, change, maintenance with a service
# window ending after/before the UX start, maintenance without window, third-party incident,
# non-MCC ticket, waiting status, problem, purchase order) and change_emergency
# (S-TICKET-025: ratchet was_emergency, initial vs non-initial timeout, the 5-positional-arg
# Oracle bug that puts p_zitadel_contact_id into the private text).
#
# Determinism: every ticket starts with ux_timeout_start = TIMESTAMP '2026-01-10 10:00:00'
# (the Oracle column is TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE, converted in the +00:00 session), so each
# timeout is a fixed wall-clock value; the steps record day/hour of CAST(ux_timeout AS
# TIMESTAMP) right after each call (the same ticket is recomputed several times). The
# service-window branch compares the WALL CLOCK: Oracle re-labels end_date with
# from_tz(..., 'EUROPE/ZURICH') and adds 60 minutes to that, the translation adds 60 minutes
# to the plain timestamp -- CAST(... AS TIMESTAMP) shows the same wall clock on both sides
# (the instants differ by the Zurich offset only because the container runs in UTC; see
# README "Timezone").
#
# known.diff: S-TICKET-059 again (change_emergency writes through add_status_change_event:
# Oracle company_id NULL, translation = ticket company); the last probe isolates it. The
# deferral event goes through event_interface.addevent_new and carries a company on both.
#
# ORA_USER=system: fixtures in stop.company, stop.contact, mss.host, mss.service,
# mss.host2service; TT holds only SELECT on those. Rolled back at the end.
ORA_USER=system
COMMITS=no
COMPARE_MSG=no
DESCRIPTION=change_deferral_date, update_ux_timeout_for_ticket (all timeout branches), change_emergency on tickets 952210-952221
